        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A battery snow blower is now the right machine for most one- and two-car driveways in areas with ordinary winters: it starts every time, needs almost no maintenance, and clears typical storms without trouble. Keep the batteries indoors and buy the larger packs, and it will rarely let you down.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Gas still earns its place on long driveways, gravel, heavy-snow regions and streets with a regular plow berm. If that describes your winters, buy a gas two-stage, or a battery two-stage if you can accept the price, and size it to your worst regular storm rather than your average one.
          </p>
